From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:47:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement
 wlr-foreign-toplevel-management-unstable-v1

Add a zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1 global (version 3) so that task
bars, docks and window switchers can list the open windows and control
them.

Every window gets a foreign toplevel when it is created. It is announced
to each bound manager as a zwlr_foreign_toplevel_handle_v1 once the
window is mapped, if it is a normal, dialog or utility window that is
neither override redirect nor a layer surface, and closed when the
window is unmanaged or stops qualifying.

Each handle gets the title, the app_id (the window's WM class, which is
the xdg_toplevel app_id for Wayland clients), the outputs the window
overlaps, the maximized/minimized/activated/fullscreen state and, for
transient windows, the parent handle. Window changes mark the toplevel
dirty and an idle flush sends what changed, followed by one done event.

Requests map onto window operations: activate -> meta_window_activate(),
close -> meta_window_delete(), set/unset_maximized,
set/unset_minimized, set/unset_fullscreen (moving the window to the
requested output first) and set_rectangle -> the window's icon geometry.
What a request changes is sent right away, in the same dispatch, and
pending changes are flushed before the finished event of a stopped
manager, so a client that sends a request and stops the manager (as
wlrctl does) gets the result before finished.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
